# Tools stay IN the repo: they regenerate the icon and Mr. Yeeper's
# portrait, so losing them means losing the ability to change the art.
# .pkgmeta already strips them from the CurseForge zip, which is the
# thing that actually needed them gone.

# Generated art source and output, kept out of the addon zip by .pkgmeta
# but useful in the repo.

# Editor / agent scratch. Skills are the exception: yeeper-voice and its
# line bank are authored work, not scratch, and losing them to a clean
# would cost real effort. Same argument as Tools above -- .pkgmeta already
# strips .claude from the CurseForge zip, which is the part that actually
# needed it gone, so it can live in the repo safely.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# Scraper page cache. Re-running a parser should be free; refetching 80
# Wowhead pages to test a regex is how you earn a 403.
Tools/.cache/

# Python bytecode. Regenerated on every run and versioned by interpreter
# version, so a committed .pyc is pure diff noise that never merges.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
